      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "TSO Mou-ti 左懋第 (T. 仲及, H. 蘿石), 1601–1645, Aug., Ming official and martyr, was a native of Laiyang, Shantung. He became a chin-shih in 1631, was made a prefect of Han-ch'êng, Shensi, and later supervising censor of the Board of Revenue in which capacity he pleaded earnestly for relief of the people from burdensome taxes and military levies.",
          "source": "eccp-3658525",
